name sat-12-duel-gate-1
timeout 460
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; the criteria: doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2.
#
# WHAT IS NEW AGAINST `sat-09-gate-strike`, WHICH THIS FILE IS THE FLIGHT-IDENTICAL TWIN OF: BOTH SIDES
# ARE GRADED. `sat-09` gives its four MiG-29 one `survive until 260` each and their outcome class is
# then (12, 4) on EVERY allele of their whole strategy space — a constant (E-30). This file adds a rung
# ladder to the RED side, four more to the BLUE side, and changes no coordinate, no store and no brief.
#
# THE ADDITION COSTS NO PHYSICS, MEASURED: an `objective` is read by the judge and by nobody else, so
# against `sat-09` under the same binary all 20 telemetry files are PREFIX-IDENTICAL and the eight blue
# `UNIT_RESULT` lines are unchanged (SUCCESS x 8). What changes is the verdict of the four MiG-29
# (SUCCESS -> TIMEOUT) and, because a unit that has not concluded keeps the run open, the duration:
# 260.1 s -> 460.0 s, exit 0 -> 3. Nothing graded moved with it — every span here closes at t = 260.
#
# THE MARGIN, IN THE HEAD, AS A NUMBER, ONCE PER SIDE. Every graded quantity is either a
# declared-cylinder DWELL or a PLANAR MIN-RANGE between two named units; every rung sits in a MEASURED
# gap of its own quantity's lever spectrum, quoted against the chaos amplitude of THAT quantity over
# the +-3 m spawn grid, taken as the WORSE of the two perturbations (one's own and the opponent's).
#
#   RED  narrowest 11.9x — `cp1`'s min-range to `es3`, 117.6 m against a chaos amplitude of 9.90 m.
#        Widest 43.3x. Four ladders, 21 rungs, one per MiG-29, each against ONE named escort.
#   BLUE narrowest 12.0x — `es3`'s min-range to `cp2`, 122.6 m against 10.20 m; the other three new
#        ladders run 12.3 / 28.6 / 95.8x. The 14 inherited `avoid zone` rungs have a chaos amplitude of
#        0.000 s over the whole grid, so their ratio is unbounded and the absolute distance to the
#        nearest measured dwell is quoted instead: 0.40 / 0.50 / 0.80 s.
#   The RELEASE GATE is unchanged and is still the primary structural device: `ccip-tight` takes the
#        package from 4 releases to 0, and the aim points sit at the fixed point of their own release
#        lattice (baseline impact 0.0 m, the bias rails +-23.7 m against a 45 m fail radius, 21.3 m of
#        margin), so `bias-early`/`bias-late` stay INERT — 4a satisfied rather than evaded.
#
# WHY BLUE WAS RE-LADDERED, and it is a finding rather than a tuning: `E20`'s emission seam (`duels.md`
# D3e) moved every MiG-29 briefed a GCI range beyond its own 50 km reach, and this CAP is one. Measured
# with the two binaries side by side on `sat-09` ITSELF, same instrument, same lever file: blue went
# from **9 distinct classes, 52.0 % modal, 12 movers** (`E18` 3's committed table, reproduced to the
# digit) to **5 distinct, 68.0 %, 8 movers** — S1 REFUSED. The four min-range ladders restore the
# ceiling: 12 of the 24 levers are the identity map on any F-16 side, so 12 movers is the maximum and
# 13 of 25 = 52.0 % the lowest modal share this lever file allows.
#
# THE SCRAMBLE: each escort names one MiG-29 and each MiG-29 names one escort, and the two maps are
# NOT inverse to each other — no ladder is satisfied by the pairing a briefed sort contract produces.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (tools/fb_duel_arena.py, `--elev const`):
#   BLUE, 24 levers of tools/levers-campaign-g5.txt: BASELINE (21, 45), 11 distinct classes, modal
#     share 52.0 % (13 of 25), S7 0 of 8 on all ten (cell, red) pairs. live G1 shape 6 of 6, G5 emcon
#     3 of 3, G3 net 1 of 2, G7 ccip 1 of 2, G6 bias 1 of 3 (`bias-rail` only — no delivery at all, NOT
#     a direction); INERT G2 cover and G4 energy, by airframe and by task. 12 movers of 24, the ceiling.
#   RED, 9 levers of tools/levers-red-mig29.txt (the alphabet a MiG-29 can express, E-31): BASELINE
#     (8, 15), 7 distinct classes, modal share 40.0 % (4 of 10), S7 0 of 8 on all 25 (cell, blue) pairs.
#     live G5 emcon 2 of 5, G3 sort 4 of 4 — 6 movers of 9, 5 of them off their band's rail.
#     `emcon-tight`, `emcon-mid` and `emcon-lo` are the identity map here because the PUR-31 gate is
#     `f x 27.0 nm` against briefed GCI calls, and all three land on the same side of every threshold.
#
# ONE ASYMMETRY WITH ITS SISTER FILES, AND IT IS REPORTED BECAUSE IT IS LUCK RATHER THAN DESIGN: the
# blue rungs here were placed under the ONE-OPPONENT rule (`E18` 1b) and passed the per-opponent screen
# anyway — 0 of 8 on all ten pairs, first time of asking. `sat-10` and `sat-11` did not, and had to be
# re-placed against the whole opponent space. Nothing here was tightened afterwards; the difference is
# that this geometry's escorts pass their MiG at ranges whose spectrum is sparse under every allele.
#
# AND THE CLOCK, because X-7 is the trap: the run duration is 460.0 s on ALL 35 runs of both lever sets
# — one value, no spread at all. `sat-09`'s two values are gone for the same reason its exit code
# changed: red now carries objectives it does not meet, so nobody concludes early.
#
# THE ARENA: a four-ship CCIP strike at 900 m on four soft aim points, escorted by a dry four-ship
# against a dry four-ship MiG-29 CAP under a GCI brief. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking
# (C4). Every coordinate is [SET] except the four aim points. Day, 11:00 local.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION, ASKED OF BOTH SEATS: WITH NEITHER FIGHTER ABLE TO SHOOT, DOES EACH SIDE'S
# DOCTRINE GET IT TO THE OPPONENT IT WAS NAMED FOR — AND DOES THE ESCORT'S SHAPE STILL LET THE STRIKE
# PICKLE?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log         `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE unit=st* accepted=` — the release decision; `mission
#                      WINDOW_CLOSED` at t = 260.1; `mission IDENTIFIED`; `zone ENTER`/`EXIT`
#   telemetry_es*.csv  `zone_zg1_s`, `zone_zg2_s`, `zone_zg3_s`, `flt_src`, `flt_assign`
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the ONLY exit this file produces and is NOT the
# measurement. THE MEASUREMENT IS TWO OUTCOME CLASSES — (V, M) summed over the eight F-16 and (V, M)
# summed over the four MiG-29 — AND THE SPREAD OF EACH ACROSS ITS OWN LEVER SET. They are never
# compared with each other. A single run measures NOTHING.


zone zg1 33.24000 44.44000 9000 0 12000

zone zg2 33.24000 44.60000 6000 0 12000

zone zg3 33.32000 44.60000 4000 0 12000

unit es1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight es 1
  spawn 33.36000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.36000 45.00000 6000 480
